title: 'pallet-whitelist: permissionless authorized dispatch'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `dispatch_whitelisted_call` and `dispatch_whitelisted_call_with_preimage` gain
    `#[pallet::authorize]` callbacks: an unsigned submission is admitted at the transaction
    pool if `DispatchWhitelistedOrigin::try_origin(Authorized)` passes and the call hash is in
    `WhitelistedCall`. `frame_system::AuthorizeCall` converts the `None` origin into
    `Authorized` for the dispatch body. Dispatch bodies are unchanged and no new `Config` item
    is added. `WeightInfo` gains `authorize_*` functions for the authorization weights.

    Every way these calls can fail at dispatch fails with nobody charged, so both witnesses are
    checked at the pool: `dispatch_whitelisted_call` fetches the preimage at `call_encoded_len`
    and decodes it to reject a `call_weight_witness` below the call's weight. Submissions are
    tagged `(call_hash, call_encoded_len, call_weight)`, so the two calls share a slot when they
    witness the same values.

    Adds `frame_system::EnsureAuthorized`. A runtime opts in by including it in
    `DispatchWhitelistedOrigin`, e.g. `EitherOf<EnsureRoot<AccountId>, EnsureAuthorized<AccountId>>`;
    leaving it out keeps the current behavior.

